 "assumptions": [
  {
   "id": "A1",
   "text": "SeededEntropy (repeatable randomness for the web preview and the fake product's differential test, never for tokens) counts as a test double, so it moves into kkt-entropy behind `testing`, not to an implementation crate."
  },
  {
   "id": "A2",
   "text": "kkt-service's DryRun wraps another System and only prints what it would do; it is the crate's own logic over its contract, not a real implementation, so it stays."
  },
  {
   "id": "A3",
   "text": "The program kkt counts as a consumer when its code names a trait (for example Box<dyn watch::Server>), as the definition says; kkt-watch::Server's one consumer is the program."
  },
  {
   "id": "A4",
   "text": "\"The record types Reads and Writes use\" is taken as the 36 public types of kkt-store that the two traits' methods name (32), or that appear inside those types (AgentLaneRecord, ChannelNoteRecord, LaneSourceRecord) or inside StoreResult (StoreError). ChannelKind, the 16 channel kinds the tests go through, appears in neither trait, so it stays in kkt-store."
  },
  {
   "id": "A5",
   "text": "kkt-rules no longer names kkt-store's Db: its Deps and CommandLine take a store meeting its Reads and Writes, which is the program's adapter over kkt-store's Db. How it opens a transaction on that store is left to the refactor."
  }
 ],
